{"tool": "revise", "arguments": {"initiative": "shared-integrations", "node": "49512a14-d828-595f-abe9-19ac7c64277d", "patch": {"body": "The local webhook fixture now verifies SHA-256 HMAC signatures against all configured active keys before parsing raw request bytes, supporting the documented rotation overlap. It validates payload size and object shape, retries processing three times with exponential backoff, avoids exception/payload logging, and raises DeliveryFailed on exhaustion rather than dropping deliveries. Eight unittest checks pass. The API now requires raw bytes, signature and signing_keys. Billing readiness still requires confirming the provider wire signature format, an HTTP adapter with bounded request reads and retryable failure responses or durable retention, and an idempotent processor; these integrations are absent from this fixture."}}, "response": {"api_version": 1, "data": {"affected": [], "artifacts": [], "changes": [{"after": "The local webhook fixture now verifies SHA-256 HMAC signatures against all configured active keys before parsing raw request bytes, supporting the documented rotation overlap. It validates payload size and object shape, retries processing three times with exponential backoff, avoids exception/payload logging, and raises DeliveryFailed on exhaustion rather than dropping deliveries. Eight unittest checks pass. The API now requires raw bytes, signature and signing_keys. Billing readiness still requires confirming the provider wire signature format, an HTTP adapter with bounded request reads and retryable failure responses or durable retention, and an idempotent processor; these integrations are absent from this fixture.", "before": "Our webhook receiver retries failed deliveries three times with a short\nbackoff. Beyond that, deliveries are dropped and logged.\n", "field": "body"}, {"after": ["kind:episode", "role:revised", "lang:en", "topic:webhook", "topic:local", "topic:webhook-retry-local-note", "topic:retry", "topic:no